error[NK1336]: `pick` hands back a view, but has no body to tell whose data it points into, and no `from`.
  --> tests/a_trait_method_with_a_view_result_and_no_from_is_refused.nika:4:5
   |
 4 |     fn pick(a: ref String, b: ref String) -> ref String
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: Where there is no body to infer it from - a trait's method, a foreign function - `from` alone makes the result a view of what it names, and a result without one owns its value (ADR-views-3 D8, D14).
   = help: Write one of `from a`, `from b`, `from a | b` after the result type, or declare it without `ref` to hand back text of its own.
